.TH PYATCLI 1 "" "PyATCLI 2026.11.2" "PyATCLI"
.SH NAME
pyatcli \- analyse fibre-photometry, NIRS and tabular recordings from a script or the shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pyatcli
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B python \-m PyATCLI
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the analyses of PyAT (Python Analysis Tool) on a recording without the app, writes their tables and a provenance record, and runs an analysis again from its record to check the numbers. Standard output is only ever the result (\-\-json for a program, \-\-plain for tab\-separated rows); warnings, errors and progress go to standard error.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
run one analysis on a recording
.TP
.B reproduce
run an analysis again from its provenance record and check the numbers
.TP
.B batch
run many analyses over many recordings
.TP
.B group
group analysis across recordings: setup (the wizard) and run
.TP
.B group setup
set up a group analysis as the wizard does, and write its analysis_settings.json
.TP
.B group run
run a group analysis from its analysis_settings.json
.TP
.B saved
edit what the app's Save Changes saves (markers, splices, signal names, highlights, text)
.TP
.B saved show
list what is saved for a recording
.TP
.B saved marker
Add Marker + Save Changes: put a marker at a time (seconds, on the time axis as the recording now stands)
.TP
.B saved unmark
delete the saved markers near a time
.TP
.B saved splice
Splice + Save Changes: stack a splice on the saved ones (it is replayed whenever the recording opens)
.TP
.B saved unsplice
take one saved splice out of the stack
.TP
.B saved rename
give signals names of your own, kept with the recording
.TP
.B saved highlight
Highlighter + Save Changes: shade a stretch of the recording
.TP
.B saved text
Text tool + Save Changes: put a text box on the plot
.TP
.B saved clear
Undo All Changes, saved: delete every file in the recording's JSON saves folder (asks first)
.TP
.B kinds
list the analyses and their parameters
.TP
.B info
versions of this library, Python and the numerical packages
.TP
.B serve
the engine: these operations as JSON lines on stdin/stdout, with recordings kept open
.TP
.B docs
print this command line's reference: markdown, or a man page (or the engine's contract)
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Accepted before or after the command name.
.TP
.B \-\-json
print the result as one JSON document on stdout
.TP
.B \-\-plain
print tab\-separated rows on stdout, nothing else (for cut, awk, spreadsheets)
.TP
.B \-\-quiet, \-q
print nothing but errors
.TP
.B \-\-verbose, \-v
say more on stderr (and show what libraries print)
.TP
.B \-\-debug, \-d
show the full traceback of an error (also set by DEBUG=1)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-input
never ask a question (an action that needs a yes fails instead)
.TP
.B \-\-events
report progress, warnings and notes as JSON lines on stderr (for a program driving this one)
.TP
.B \-\-progress
always show a progress bar on stderr for slow steps
.TP
.B \-\-no\-progress
never show a progress bar (the default shows one when stderr is a terminal)
.SH RUN
run one analysis on a recording
.PP
.B python \-m PyATCLI run [options] kind recording
.TP
.I kind
the analysis (see kinds)
.TP
.I recording
a TDT folder, an Oxysoft .txt export, or a generic table file
.TP
.B \-\-param, \-p NAME=VALUE
an analysis parameter; repeat for several
.TP
.B \-\-params FILE.json
parameters from a JSON file, or \- for standard input (\-\-param overrides it)
.TP
.B \-\-out, \-o DIR
folder for the CSV tables and the provenance record (default pyatcli\-output)
.TP
.B \-\-output\-folder DIR
an Output folder, laid out as PyAT's exports are: <DIR>/<data type>/<recording> (Analysis)/, and a repeat run never overwrites an earlier one
.TP
.B \-\-regression REGRESSION
motion\-correction method for TDT (default ols)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-saved
ignore the recording's saved splices and markers (JSON saves/)
.TP
.B \-\-table TABLE
generic file: which table to open
.TP
.B \-\-x X
generic file: the x column (default the first)
.TP
.B \-\-y Y ...
generic file: the trace columns (default all the others)
.PP
Examples:
.nf
python \-m PyATCLI run event_peth "D:/rats/Rat7\-250101" \-\-param event="L1P¹" \-\-param pre_s=10 \-\-param post_s=20 \-\-out out
python \-m PyATCLI run zscore_window "D:/rats/Rat7\-250101" \-\-param center_s=312.5 \-\-param signal=main_driver \-\-json
python \-m PyATCLI run auc_window recording.txt \-p center_s=30 \-\-output\-folder Output   # Output/Oxysoft/recording (Analysis)/
.fi
.SH REPRODUCE
run an analysis again from its provenance record and check the numbers
.PP
.B python \-m PyATCLI reproduce [options] record
.TP
.I record
a .provenance.json written beside an export, or \- for standard input
.TP
.B \-\-recording RECORDING
where the recording is now, if it is not where the record says
.TP
.B \-\-compare, \-c EXPORT.csv ...
exports to check the result against
.TP
.B \-\-tolerance TOLERANCE
|a\-b| <= tolerance*(1+|b|) counts as equal (default 1e\-4)
.TP
.B \-\-strict
fail if the recording or the software differs from the record's
.TP
.B \-\-rounded
the exports hold rounded numbers: accept the digits they show (the default for PyAT's exports)
.TP
.B \-\-exact
compare to the tolerance only, whoever wrote the exports
.TP
.B \-\-out, \-o DIR
write the result tables and a new record here
.PP
Examples:
.nf
python \-m PyATCLI reproduce "out/Rat7_event_peth.provenance.json" \-\-compare "out/Event PETH.csv"
python \-m PyATCLI reproduce record.provenance.json \-\-recording "E:/moved/Rat7" \-\-strict
.fi
.SH BATCH
run many analyses over many recordings
.PP
.B python \-m PyATCLI batch [options] jobs
.TP
.I jobs
JSON: {"defaults": {...}, "jobs": [{"kind", "recording", "parameters"}, ...]}, or \- for standard input
.TP
.B \-\-out, \-o DIR
folder for the results, a folder per job and recording (default pyatcli\-batch)
.TP
.B \-\-output\-folder DIR
an Output folder, laid out as PyAT's exports are: <DIR>/<data type>/<recording> (Analysis)/, and a repeat run never overwrites an earlier one
.TP
.B \-\-regression REGRESSION
motion\-correction method for TDT (default ols)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-saved
ignore the recording's saved splices and markers (JSON saves/)
.TP
.B \-\-table TABLE
generic file: which table to open
.TP
.B \-\-x X
generic file: the x column (default the first)
.TP
.B \-\-y Y ...
generic file: the trace columns (default all the others)
.PP
Examples:
.nf
python \-m PyATCLI batch jobs.json \-\-out batch\-out
python \-m PyATCLI batch jobs.json \-\-output\-folder Output
cat jobs.json | python \-m PyATCLI batch \- \-\-out batch\-out
.fi
.SH GROUP
Group analysis (Hypothesis Testing): group setup finds the recordings, lists the markers they share and writes analysis_settings.json; group run runs it.
.PP
.B python \-m PyATCLI group <setup|run> [options]
.PP
Examples:
.nf
python \-m PyATCLI group setup "D:/cohort" \-\-name Sucrose                       # lists the markers the recordings share
python \-m PyATCLI group setup "D:/cohort" \-\-name Sucrose \-\-marker "L1P¹" \-\-marker "L2P¹" \-\-output\-folder Output
python \-m PyATCLI group run "Output/Group Analysis/Sucrose"
.fi
.SH GROUP SETUP
Finds the recordings (a cohort folder is searched, at any depth), lists the markers they share, takes the choices the wizard asks for, checks the design and writes analysis_settings.json. Without \-\-marker it only lists the markers. The defaults are the wizard's.
.PP
.B python \-m PyATCLI group setup [options] folders ...
.TP
.I folders
a cohort folder to search, or recordings (TDT blocks)
.TP
.B \-\-name NAME
the group's name (its folder and its figures' titles)
.TP
.B \-\-marker, \-m NAME
a marker to compare, as group setup lists it; repeat for each
.TP
.B \-\-exclude RECORDING
leave a recording out, by its subject name; repeat
.TP
.B \-\-store\-label ID=NAME
show an event store under another name (what Edit Attributes does); repeat
.TP
.B \-\-pre PRE
seconds before each event (default 10)
.TP
.B \-\-post POST
seconds after each event (default 10)
.TP
.B \-\-baseline START END
the baseline window, seconds from the event (default (\-10.0, \-6.0))
.TP
.B \-\-response START END
the response window, seconds from the event (default (0.0, 10.0))
.TP
.B \-\-signal SIGNAL
dff, or zscore (also divide by the baseline's SD)
.TP
.B \-\-smooth SMOOTH
moving\-average smoothing before slicing, seconds; 0 for none (default 0.5)
.TP
.B \-\-measure MEASURE
a measure to compute and test; repeat (default: all five)
.TP
.B \-\-peak\-direction PEAK_DIRECTION
default absolute
.TP
.B \-\-decay\-fraction DECAY_FRACTION
how far the trace must fall for the decay time, as a fraction of the peak (default 0.5)
.TP
.B \-\-correction CORRECTION
multiple\-comparison correction (default holm)
.TP
.B \-\-alpha ALPHA
significance level (default 0.05)
.TP
.B \-\-regression REGRESSION
motion\-correction method for every recording (default ols)
.TP
.B \-\-out, \-o DIR
folder for the settings (and, with \-\-run, the results)
.TP
.B \-\-output\-folder DIR
an Output folder, laid out as PyAT's exports are: <DIR>/Group Analysis/<group name>, a new folder if the name was used before
.TP
.B \-\-run
run the analysis right after, as the wizard's Run Analysis does
.PP
Examples:
.nf
python \-m PyATCLI group setup "D:/cohort" \-\-name Sucrose
python \-m PyATCLI group setup "D:/cohort" \-\-name Sucrose \-\-marker "L1P¹" \-\-marker "L2P¹" \-\-output\-folder Output \-\-run
.fi
.SH GROUP RUN
run a group analysis from its analysis_settings.json
.PP
.B python \-m PyATCLI group run [options] settings
.TP
.I settings
analysis_settings.json, or the folder holding it
.TP
.B \-\-out, \-o DIR
folder for the tables and the report
.TP
.B \-\-output\-folder DIR
an Output folder, laid out as PyAT's exports are: <DIR>/Group Analysis/<group name>, a new folder if the name was used before
.PP
Examples:
.nf
python \-m PyATCLI group run "Output/Group Analysis/Sucrose"
python \-m PyATCLI group run analysis_settings.json \-\-out results
.fi
.SH SAVED
Writes the files PyAT writes in a recording's JSON saves folder, so what is done here is what was done in the app: either reads it back when it opens the recording.
.PP
.B python \-m PyATCLI saved <show|marker|unmark|splice|unsplice|rename|highlight|text|clear> [options]
.PP
Examples:
.nf
python \-m PyATCLI saved show "D:/rats/Rat7"
python \-m PyATCLI saved marker "D:/rats/Rat7" \-\-time 312.5 \-\-label Lever
python \-m PyATCLI saved splice "D:/rats/Rat7" \-\-mode cut_out \-\-start 40 \-\-end 55
python \-m PyATCLI saved clear "D:/rats/Rat7"          # asks first; \-\-yes to go ahead without asking
.fi
